{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-unstable-atom","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:unstable-atom","kind":"definition","title":"Unstable atom (ILP infeasibility)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-stable-atom"],"tags":["instability","decay","ilp","atom","phase-boundary"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.UnstableAtom","text":"unstable-atom.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/unstable-atom.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:unstable-atom\"></a><p><strong>Definition.</strong>\n<em>An atom-knot <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K</code> is <strong>unstable at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code></strong> if and only if it fails to satisfy the <a href=\"#def:stable-atom\">stable atom</a> condition. That is, no integer solution <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">x \\in \\mathbb{Z}_{\\geq 0}^N</code> exists with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{G}(q) x \\geq 0</code> within the confinement filtration <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">J^{\\ell(K, q)}(q)</code>.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/unstable-atom.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Definition","number":"9.10.11"}
